# Project: Servezy — Zero-Commission QR Restaurant SaaS
# Role: Senior full-stack engineer. Production-grade, multi-tenant, security-first.

## Before Writing Any Code
- Read docs/02-database-schema.md for exact models. Never invent new fields.
- Read docs/03-api-spec.md for endpoint contracts. Match them exactly.
- Read docs/04-ui-design-system.md before generating ANY UI component.

## Tech Stack (never deviate)
- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript strict + Socket.io + Mongoose + Zod.
- Customer PWA: Next.js (App Router) + Tailwind + Zustand on Vercel.
- Staff app: Expo + NativeWind + expo-router + socket.io-client.
- No other state libs, CSS frameworks, or UI kits unless docs specify.

## Multi-Tenancy Rules (CRITICAL)
- Every collection except `Restaurant` and `SubscriptionPayment` has `restaurantId`.
- Every find/update/delete includes `restaurantId: req.tenant._id`. No exceptions.
- Tenant comes from verified JWT (staff) or :tenantSlug (public). NEVER from req.body.
- Socket.io: rooms are `kitchen_{restaurantId}`. Membership derived from
  server-verified JWT only. Never trust a client-sent room name. Never broadcast globally.

## Security Rules (CRITICAL)
- Zod validates every request body/params/query. Reject unknown fields.
- bcrypt salt 10 for passwords. Staff PINs hashed too.
- JWT: HTTP-only secure cookie (web) / expo-secure-store (native). Never localStorage.
- Order totals computed server-side from MenuItem.price. Client cannot send price.
- Rate limit auth + order routes (key: tenantId + IP).
- Subscription guard: expired restaurant → 402 on ordering/staff APIs. Owner panel
  stays reachable so they can renew.

## Code Style
- Strict TypeScript. No `any`. No non-null assertions except Mongoose lean results.
- Thin routes → services/ holds business logic → models/ holds schemas only.
- All Express handlers wrapped in asyncHandler; central error handler in app.ts.
- Components: function components + hooks. No classes. No inline styles (web).
- Every endpoint returns consistent shape: { success, data } or { success: false, error, details? }.

## UI Quality Rules (this app must NOT look AI-generated)
- Follow docs/04-ui-design-system.md exactly: font, spacing scale, radius, shadows.
- Use the design tokens. No default Tailwind blue. No purple gradients. No emoji icons —
  use lucide-react (web) / lucide-react-native (app).
- Every interactive element needs: hover state, active state, loading state, empty state.
- Lists need skeletons, not spinners. Tables need sticky headers. Forms need inline validation.
- Whitespace is a feature: use the 4/8px spacing scale. Dense ≠ good.
- KDS is glanceable from 3 meters: huge type, high contrast, no decoration.
